//! The `font-synthesis-style` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property lets
//! you specify whether or not the browser may synthesize the oblique typeface when it is missing in
//! a font family.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | none | oblique-only
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4/#propdef-font-synthesis-style
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-synthesis-style
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

